    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d342">

                <pb facs="0372" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg312"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Eustis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-22"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Would not French citizen maltreated on voyage, as Waller alleges himself to have
                    been, have right to sue French Government for damages as well as private
                    individuals? If there is doubt on the point take Clunet’s opinion. In this
                    connection, was or was not Waller during voyage in custody of ship or of French
                    military authorities? Cable answer.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
